  "text": "\n     Election Information • Durham, NH \n Skip to Main Content \r\n     Our Community   \t\t\t \n     Doing Business   \t\t\t \n     Inside Town Hall   \t\t\t \n     Helpful Resources   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \nHome \n                News Flash\nElection Information \nNews Flash \n            Election Information\n                News & Updates\n                Posted on August 05, 2026 \nAbsentee Ballots - Click  HERE \nSample Ballots - Click  HERE \nRegistering to Vote? Click  HERE \nWhere Do I Vote? Click  HERE    \nElection Dates/Public Notices- Click  HERE \nStudent Voting- Click  HERE   \nPlease be advised that the United States District Court for the District of New Hampshire has ordered the State of New Hampshire not to enforce the portions of HB 1569 that eliminated the qualified voter affidavit as a means of proving citizenship and the challenged voter affidavit as a procedural safeguard for challenged voters. Effective immediately, the Secretary of State's Office is implementing the Court's order. \nAs an initial step, voters who lack documentary proof of citizenship, such as a birth certificate or passport, may use the updated qualified voter affidavit form to establish citizenship for voter registration purposes. \nPlease note that the Court's order does not affect the portions of HB 1569 requiring documentary proof of identity, age, and domicile. Affidavits may not be used to establish identity, age, or domicile. The order also does not affect the requirement that voters present proof of identity when checking in to receive a ballot on Election Day. Voters who do not have acceptable identification on Election Day may not use a challenged voter affidavit to establish identity and obtain a ballot. \nThank you for your patience and flexibility as we continue to assess the impact of the Court's order and consult with the Attorney General's Office in preparation for upcoming elections. Please watch for additional communications, as further guidance may be forthcoming. \nRelated News \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAutomated Curbside Solid Waste and Recycling Collection Information 2026\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNews & Updates\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPosted on August 05, 2026 \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTRAFFIC/CONSTRUCTION ADVISORY – Madbury Road between Hampshire Avenue and Lundy Lane\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNews & Updates\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPosted on August 05, 2026 \n\t\t\t Town GIS Map \r\n\t\t\t Agendas & Minutes \r\n\t\t\t DCAT Media on Demand \r\n\t\t\t Online Payments \r\n\t\t\t Recreation \r\n\t\t\t Trash & Recycling \r\nContact Us \r\n8 Newmarket Rd \nDurham, NH 03824 \r\nPhone:  603-868-5571 \r\nQuick Links \r\n         Calendar \n         Directory \n         Subscribe \n         Welcome Visitors \n         Sustainable Durham \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\nSite Links \r\n         Home \n         Sign In \n         Site Map \n         Contact Us \n         Accessibility \n         Copyright Notices \n         Privacy Policy \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right \r\n[] \r\n                     Slideshow Left Arrow \r\n                     Slideshow Right Arrow \r\n ",
